# P6 situational eval traces. 15 entries, ground-truth action label per entry.
#
# Assessment mode: A (independent). Each eval trace assessed against the initial seed-group state from seed_groups.jsonl.
# The harness MUST reset group state to the seed snapshot between eval ingests (not cumulative across the eval set).
# Cumulative-mode evaluation is a separate fixture, deferred.
#
# DB isolation: situational corpus runs in its own probe DB (separate from probe_eval / islands).
# Entity names here are disjoint from islands to keep the corpus robust if isolation breaks.
#
# Action distribution — deliberately oversampled on action≠none for measurement signal:
#   extend=5, revise=3, create=1, none=6.
# Real-world prior is 70–80% none per situational.default.md base-rate guidance; this corpus is a measurement instrument, not a traffic sample.
# Aggregate none-rate gate must derive from this fixture's ground-truth distribution (40% none), not the prior.
#
# expected_group_id  references seed_groups.jsonl when expected_action ∈ {extend, revise}.
# expected_linked_trace_ids references seed_traces.jsonl when expected_action = create.
# expected_implication / expected_situation / expected_significance follow situational.default.md output spec.

